      "message": "I don\u0027t think I understand the point of this change.  rebatch does not go through this code path -- this is called only for incoming new alarms.  Furthermore, if triggerAtTime is in the past, advancing it by a constant 5 seconds is not a meaningful adjustment.  It\u0027s surprisingly common for triggerAtTime to be zero, for example: if an app wants to have an alarm fire as soon as possible this is more efficient than calculating \u0027now\u0027 just to set the alarm.",
