      "message": "Hi Chris, \n\nI know the re-batch logic is not at here, but re-batch will be affected by this parameter-\"triggerAtTime\". \n\nWhile adding a new alarm, this new alarm\u0027s parameter-\"origWhen\" will be assigned this value - \"triggerAtTime\". \n\nSo let go to see see the re-batch function.\n\nvoid reAddAlarmLocked(Alarm a, long nowElapsed, boolean doValidate) {\na.when \u003d a.origWhen;\n(...skip)\n\nSo if once reAddAlarmLocked function triggers, this new alarm\u0027s parameter-\"when\" will be assigned back this value \"origWhen\".\n\n\nSo this patch is to fix the defect.",
